target:    tests/docker/canary/compute-canary-verdict.py
gate:      composer test:canary-verdict
kind:      guard-narrowing
expect:    right subject, wrong relation: expected MISSED, got CAUGHT
rationale: Drops the relation term from the detection match, so naming the pre-declared report under ANY of the eight relations counts as a catch. CANARY-C1.md requires both -- the subject AND the defect -- and this is precisely how that rule erodes in practice: the subject is the memorable half, the relation reads like taxonomy, and an adjudicator that said 'top_resource: value-differs' about a report that lost a row looks close enough to a reader who already knows the answer. Under the mutation an agent that identified the wrong defect in the right report is scored as having caught the canary.
---
--- a/tests/docker/canary/compute-canary-verdict.py
+++ b/tests/docker/canary/compute-canary-verdict.py
@@ -60,7 +60,6 @@
         for f in (report.get("findings") or [])
         if isinstance(f, dict)
         and f.get("subject") == subject
-        and f.get("relation") == relation
     ]
 
 
